        inputs: "**Money is the raw material.** Deposits of ₹1,794,625cr at March 2026 fund most loans; borrowings of ₹124,994cr are only about 5% of the balance sheet. A large part of the deposits sits in current and savings accounts (CASA), which pay little or no interest and are the cheapest money a bank can get; they were 39.5% of deposits at June 2026 (41.4% in March), and savings deposits grew only 6.8% in the year. **Cost of deposits was 4.41%** in Q1 FY27, down from 4.85% a year earlier. The new foreign-currency deposits will cost about 6.3–6.4% all-in, cheaper than bulk (wholesale) deposits.",
