        salesDrivers: ["**Credit demand across the economy**: management guides loan growth of 14–15% for FY27, 2–3 points above the 12–12.5% nominal GDP growth it expects. Loans grew over 18% in the year to June 2026, flattered by a weak quarter a year earlier.", "**Deposits and liquidity**: retail fixed deposits grew 14%. It refuses to pay high rates for bulk deposits and instead holds ₹3–4 lakh crore of government bonds above the legal minimum that it can run down to fund loans. It raised about $6 billion of foreign-currency deposits from Indians abroad by early August and expects about $10 billion.", "**Interest rates**: loans linked to the RBI's repo rate reprice quickly when rates change, while deposits reprice as they mature; corporate loans are being moved to its MCLR benchmark to lift yields.", "**Bad-loan cycle**: new bad loans were ₹7,046cr in Q1 FY27 (farm ₹2,600cr, small business ₹2,300cr, personal ₹2,100cr), a seasonal rise. In Q2 gross bad loans fell to 1.39%, the lowest in over two decades (74% provided for), and credit cost was about 0.22%; early-overdue loans (SMA-1 and SMA-2) rose 15% in the quarter, mostly SMA-1, more than half of which has since been repaid. About ₹28,800cr of small-business loans (half its small-business growth) are under the government credit-guarantee scheme. In a downturn this is the line that swings most.", "**Selling stakes in subsidiaries**: the SBI Funds Management listing and another planned stake sale add capital, which funds growth and softens the expected-loss (ECL) rules from April 2027."],
